{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1763 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "78cdb82086c82f2f37e60c8c7531af60e52ab59e2fe6344626522cd437a6e4d6" :edb/db-before-t 1762 :edb/db-after-t 1763 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535075 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:17:19.262Z" 13194139535075 true] [17592186096596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329899 13194139535075 true] [17592186096596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329906 13194139535075 true] [17592186096665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329913 13194139535075 true] [17592186097273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535075 true] [17592186097273 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-y-z=-1 \\\\ -2x+4y-2z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 true] [17592186097273 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n${x - 2y + z = 1; 2x - y - z =-1; - 2x + 4y - 2z =-2$\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 false] [17592186097273 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535075 true] [17592186097276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535075 true] [17592186097276 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x-y-3z=1 \\\\ 2x+2y+6z=-2 \\\\ -2x-2y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 true] [17592186097276 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n${-x - y - 3z = 1; 2x + 2y + 6z =-2; - 2x - 2y - 6z = 2$\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 false] [17592186097276 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329900 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1089 "q-131603" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-4y+7z=-4 \\\\  & -x+3y-4z=5 \\\\  & x-2y+3z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1113 #uuid "1bcacfc8-760b-5702-9297-34f70a805709" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329899 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 7 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 7 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329901 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329902 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329903 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329904 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329905 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1041 "selection" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329905 13194139535075 true] [17592186329900 1110 #uuid "a16354a9-58f5-500f-9f4b-a8a6ff20f514" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329901 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329901 1111 #uuid "010fed17-df22-5e1d-bb27-a5dfd69cba04" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329902 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329902 1111 #uuid "b1113364-061b-59df-a896-be9a17560fad" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329903 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329903 1111 #uuid "c3f8732e-e7be-5e7e-a8d4-4de651e0e90e" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329904 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329904 1111 #uuid "8e1f91ce-424d-5819-9e1e-17a040254bb6" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329905 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329905 1111 #uuid "60675cfa-567d-53f0-9c9d-b085e94e8c57" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329907 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1089 "q-131620" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=4 \\\\  & 3x-8y+5z=10 \\\\  & -2x+6y-z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1113 #uuid "0076c92d-fb02-5965-b0a4-bdf5c061df0f" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329906 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329908 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329909 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329910 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329911 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329912 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1041 "selection" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329912 13194139535075 true] [17592186329907 1110 #uuid "79c247e0-237d-56a6-a2ce-8d09f7b06ad4" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329908 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329908 1111 #uuid "016a61fa-9b50-5e71-a8b8-8d4b886186c8" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329909 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329909 1111 #uuid "292cd9a3-8ef9-5963-98b0-51459dfbaa05" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329910 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329910 1111 #uuid "212540d7-45ac-5571-808d-fc8ab7144978" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329911 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329911 1111 #uuid "e7bd333f-31b6-5b3b-947d-b3a81ce338f7" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329912 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535075 true] [17592186329912 1111 #uuid "0c9062cc-89ef-521b-8487-4d54c11dff7c" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329914 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1089 "q-74626" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z=1 \\\\ -3x-6y+6z=-3 \\\\ 2x+5y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1113 #uuid "23bca3c5-322d-5c3f-a423-fb871cdd59a3" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329913 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-10z=-1 \\\\ y+4z=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10z-1 \\\\ y=1-4z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535075 true] [17592186329914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329915 13194139535075 true] [17592186329914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329916 13194139535075 true] [17592186329914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329917 13194139535075 true] [17592186329914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329918 131